Assign every supplied stored claim to the identity whose memory it changes.

The `owner_entity` is the identity whose lasting state, plans, requirements, responsibilities, relationships, or
history the claim updates. Use only exact stable entity IDs from the completed entity plan. Choose each route in this
order:

1. Use `project_role` only when the claim explicitly assigns a continuing responsibility or accountable role to a
   Person or `you` within exactly one Project. The person is the owner and the Project is `project_entity`.
2. Otherwise use `general` when a materialized identity can own the claim. {{ ownership_policy }}
3. Use `deferred` only when no materialized identity can reliably own the claim.

{{ subject_policy }} Ordinary participation, a single completed task, or topical context uses a general route with
`relationship_kind=other` or `none`. This step chooses ownership and relationship endpoints; later fact resolution
chooses wiki sections. Return every claim exactly once as JSON matching the schema.
